/−339; 156,255 bytes / 2,028 LF; SHA-256 9a6582563d5678c5e73f6d7c1f2244df88b9880177d03e0f75ea659e05e04b92.\nAssigned diff ledgers: derive/scope U0 38,151 bytes / 456 LF, SHA f95180da8c615bba1777f5398e76e7367c95c2407ea690ef3721cf5d96edfdf8; shared/client U3 40,075 bytes / 512 LF, SHA ebc46db1cabb7fd37a19baf4b966987b3037b44b73dc2fdf6e28749cf1164f15; reader/replay U3 19,536 bytes / 350 LF, SHA b0d9cd20700fb485655c40146b3062d02ead1e1bb957f64a946631eb3d4891c5; documents U3 31,403 bytes / 257 LF, SHA f1190b54d70039a421334b7df964fbf86265976f8f837da1f72539b5978b2c57.\n\nThis fulfills only checker request 971bd62e / promise f6103964. It is not the fresh whole 156-subject ordinary I1 review, approval, adoption, source landing or implementation closure. No tests, builds, installs, repo imports, project scripts, private diagnostics, evaluator probes, provider effects or source writes were performed. Keep every original functional outcome; estimates and attributed cost observations do not reduce scope.","body":{"head":"34d3b65664072b147c3967d3fd7620c841743985","no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"Complete 34-path preliminary repair reassessment; two residuals under existing ordinary verdict and 5fc07d88, no full source approval"}}